cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Membrane Crystallization: streaming PCA with a Hebbian running average (SYNTHETIC)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/membrane-crystallization"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC. Standard-library Python package for streaming PCA: the Hebbian
  update W <- (1 - alpha) W + alpha |x><x| is an exponentially weighted
  running estimate of the observation covariance, and its top-K
  eigenvectors are its principal components (as in Oja 1982).
  "Crystallization" is a descriptive label only. Includes a Jacobi
  eigensolver for complex Hermitian matrices that handles repeated
  eigenvalues, and seeded sweeps measuring the learning curve, the
  forgetting window (about 1/alpha), residue-whiteness controls (which
  show the metric does not separate patterns from pure noise) and
  self-recreation chains, whose fidelity decays over 20 generations.
keywords:
  - "streaming-pca"
  - "hebbian-learning"
  - "covariance-estimation"
  - "eigensolver"
  - "holographic-memory"
  - "synthetic"
  - "python"
